1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,863
A trainer has to turn a procedure into
a graded course the LMS can track,

2
00:00:05,863 --> 00:00:09,862
and know the package works
before anyone uploads it.

3
00:00:09,862 --> 00:00:13,715
Scrimshaw builds the course,
drafts the first quiz

4
00:00:13,715 --> 00:00:17,414
through Fairlead,
and publishes a SCORM package.

5
00:00:17,414 --> 00:00:22,831
The procedure and the learner are
synthetic, and the LMS is a stand-in.

6
00:00:23,081 --> 00:00:24,912
It all runs on this one computer.

7
00:00:24,912 --> 00:00:28,988
Launch dot bat starts a small
PowerShell server on loopback,

8
00:00:28,988 --> 00:00:32,112
and the editor and player
run in your browser.

9
00:00:32,812 --> 00:00:38,630
Courses autosave in browser storage,
with a dot scrim file for backup.

10
00:00:39,130 --> 00:00:42,331
In: slides you build, PowerPoint,

11
00:00:42,331 --> 00:00:47,763
and media files from Capstan,
SnapShackle and TalkForge.

12
00:00:48,223 --> 00:00:53,039
Out: SCORM, xAPI, cmi5, a web page,
a storyboard and a Word handout.

13
00:00:53,646 --> 00:00:54,646
AI is optional.

14
00:00:54,646 --> 00:00:58,547
The model key sits in Lazarette,
shared to Fairlead,

15
00:00:58,547 --> 00:01:03,350
and Scrimshaw asks Fairlead for
a draft with its own client key.

16
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:06,599
There is also a command
line and a loopback API.

17
00:01:06,599 --> 00:01:11,543
Planned: handing the key
over from Lazarette directly.

18
00:01:12,107 --> 00:01:16,423
Guardrails: loopback only,
drafts are opt-in and reviewed by you,

19
00:01:16,423 --> 00:01:20,673
publishing is checked, and the
server stops when the tab closes.

20
00:01:20,923 --> 00:01:23,500
The model key lives in Lazarette,

21
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,717
the encrypted vault,
and is shared once with Fairlead.

22
00:01:27,717 --> 00:01:30,404
This footage is from the Halyard demo:

23
00:01:30,404 --> 00:01:33,303
the same key, set up once for every tool.

24
00:01:34,003 --> 00:01:36,823
Launch dot bat starts
Scrimshaw on port eighty-seven

25
00:01:36,823 --> 00:01:39,589
seventy-five, its place in
the Fleet port registry.

26
00:01:40,289 --> 00:01:42,354
Fairlead has a client named Scrimshaw,

27
00:01:42,354 --> 00:01:44,636
so its calls can be told apart in the log.

28
00:01:45,336 --> 00:01:48,287
And the page address is
allowed as a browser origin,

29
00:01:48,287 --> 00:01:50,614
because the page calls Fairlead directly.

30
00:01:51,114 --> 00:01:52,272
Start a new course and name it.

31
00:01:52,632 --> 00:01:54,045
The passing score is eighty percent.

32
00:01:54,745 --> 00:01:57,436
Drafting is off until you turn it on.

33
00:01:57,436 --> 00:02:00,835
This PC has no local model,
so I allow a cloud engine,

34
00:02:00,835 --> 00:02:03,478
and only a made-up procedure goes through.

35
00:02:03,478 --> 00:02:06,761
The client key stays in
memory for this session.

36
00:02:07,461 --> 00:02:09,448
Draft asks the model through Fairlead.

37
00:02:10,332 --> 00:02:12,172
This is the live wait, sped up.

38
00:02:12,872 --> 00:02:17,397
Three questions come back, but nothing
is in the course until I add them.

39
00:02:17,397 --> 00:02:21,652
Then I review each question and
the answer it marks correct.

40
00:02:21,652 --> 00:02:24,699
The model can be wrong,
so the author decides.

41
00:02:25,399 --> 00:02:28,859
Fairlead keeps its own log:
client Scrimshaw,

42
00:02:28,859 --> 00:02:31,704
model GPT-5 mini, status two hundred.

43
00:02:31,954 --> 00:02:36,510
Publish offers SCORM, xAPI,
a web page or the project file.

44
00:02:36,510 --> 00:02:39,067
I take SCORM one point two.

45
00:02:39,767 --> 00:02:41,888
Inside are the manifest
and the player, one file.

46
00:02:42,429 --> 00:02:45,863
The eighty percent pass mark
travels in the manifest.

47
00:02:46,373 --> 00:02:50,027
Now a learner takes it in a
stand-in LMS I wrote for this video.

48
00:02:50,027 --> 00:02:54,143
It is not a real LMS,
but it speaks the SCORM calls,

49
00:02:54,143 --> 00:02:58,577
and every call the package
makes is logged on the right.

50
00:02:58,577 --> 00:03:01,732
First attempt:
one answer wrong on purpose.

51
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:06,000
Sixty-seven percent, under the pass mark,
so the LMS is told failed.

52
00:03:06,654 --> 00:03:11,939
Retry with every answer right: a hundred
percent, and the status is passed.

53
00:03:12,458 --> 00:03:14,637
That record is the evidence.

54
00:03:14,637 --> 00:03:19,826
A real LMS is the final check: this
proves the package, not any one vendor.

55
00:03:20,131 --> 00:03:24,067
The model drafted,
a person checked every answer,

56
00:03:24,067 --> 00:03:28,564
and the result was recorded
by the LMS, here a stand-in.

57
00:03:28,564 --> 00:03:33,497
Not shown: PowerPoint import,
xAPI, cmi5 and the command line.

58
00:03:33,497 --> 00:03:36,876
No minutes-saved number is claimed.
